    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The thing is, the power calculations aren't really strong enough to justify $n=12$ for these specific claims. I'm worried that if we spend too much time on a \"limitation\" section, we're just handing them a reason to reject it. How can we present this data so it lands as a breakthrough rather than a statistical fluke?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
